{{History of Balisca}}
The '''New Araucarian League''' ({{Langx|mxi|لِيغَا أَرَاَوْكَانَا نُوِيبَا|Nuwiba Liḡa Arawkarána}}; {{Langx|bl|Nueva Liga Araucarana}}) was the [[W:Dominant-party system|dominant political party]] in Araucaria from 1853 (then the [[Maroon Confederacy]]) to its fall from power during the [[Baliscan Revolution]]. During the revolution many of its members and supporters were targeted, and ultimately [[Baliscan post-revolution exodus|fled]] or [[Right-wing insurgency in Balisca|took up arms]] against the revolutionary government taking shape. 

The LNA continued as a {{W|rump party}} amidst the revolutionary fervor, but ceased to be officially recognized following the [[1919 Confederal Convention]]. 

